  "note": "Phase 0, complete three-arm set. Pairing re-derived by the D011 rule and unchanged. Adapter defect D013.1 fixed: providers/nvidia.py read only message.content, so a reasoning candidate's null content raised in the JSON extractor and burned three retries per item before being recorded as an outage; the fix moved the fingerprint to 2b8e15b6f390 because benchmark/providers is now inside it (D013.2), so this set is deliberately non-comparable with 3bca900de60e. Every reply is journalled and fsynced before use, so a container restart resumes rather than restarts (D014); a recorded outage replays as that outage and is never re-asked, each arm pays for its own calls, and spend and elapsed carry across resumes so the frozen ceilings bound the set. Wall-clock ceiling 1200 min set from a measured 75.2 s per logical call over 8 journalled replies of this exact configuration, decided before any arm finished and before any score existed (D015); it is an operational bound on completion, not a gating threshold, and the 2400/600 call budget is unchanged.",
